    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Notice how the formal words for 'I' and 'to be' instantly give Japanese speech a formal, public polish, while the negative request pattern gives you a clean, polite way to ask someone not to do something. Until next scene—see you again.",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "muranishi",
      "t": "また会いましょう。",
      "gap": 0.3
